<h2>1. Summer Home Décor Ideas: Light, Airy, and Peaceful</h2>
The theme of summer is all about brightness, openness, and a connection with nature. Whether one owns a beach house or a country summer home, the goal is to create a warm and casual atmosphere.

<strong>Color Scheme and Materials</strong>

Choose neutral tones highlighted by deep ocean blues, sandy dunes beige, and refreshing greens to capture the essence of summer. Lightweight, breezy fabrics such as linen and cotton for upholstery, bedding, and drapes. Mix in rattan, bamboo, and distressed wood for a natural, relaxed appearance.

<strong>Furniture &amp; Layout</strong>

Simple rusticity and lack of clutter. Minimal design and informal seating plans enhance the airy feeling, helping you discover <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/how-to-make-a-narrow-london-living-room-feel-wider/">how to make a narrow London living room feel wider</a> during sunlit months. Use hammocks, daybeds, or oversized floor pillows to achieve a casual, beachy feel. Indoor outdoor living is a must! If there's room, take your living space outdoors to a patio or garden room with lounge seating and outdoor dining space.

<strong>Décor Touches</strong>

<span style="font-weight: 400;">Light linen throws, woven baskets, and glass vases of fresh flowers add a light summer feel. Coastal photography or abstract watercolour art contributes to the relaxed atmosphere. Warm, soft lighting with fairy lights or lanterns provides a whimsical summer evening ambience.</span>

Subtle <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/lighting-design/">lighting design</a> adjustments—such as switching to warmer bulbs in the evening—can instantly transition a space from daytime freshness to relaxed summer nights.

