<h2>2. Boho Room Ideas: Free-Spirited &amp; Eclectic Spaces</h2>
For those who love a mix of colours, patterns, and textures, boho room ideas offer endless inspiration. Whether you’re decorating a bedroom, living room, or a holiday rental, boho décor brings warmth and personality to any space.

<strong>Layered Textures &amp; Patterns</strong>
<ul>
 	<li>The more textures, the better! Macramé wall hangings, shaggy rugs, fringed cushions, and beaded curtains create a tactile, inviting atmosphere.</li>
 	<li>Mix and match patterns—Moroccan prints, floral motifs, and geometric designs work beautifully together in a boho setting.</li>
</ul>
<strong>Furniture &amp; Layout</strong>
<ul>
 	<li>A boho room should feel relaxed and inviting. Low-level seating, such as floor cushions and pouffes, enhances the laid-back vibe.</li>
 	<li>Vintage and second-hand furniture add character—look for hand-carved wooden tables, distressed cabinets, and woven rattan chairs.</li>
</ul>
<strong>Décor Elements</strong>
<ul>
 	<li>Hanging plants and oversized leafy greens bring a natural touch.</li>
 	<li>Layered rugs in varying textures and colours add warmth and depth to the space.</li>
 	<li>A mix of candles, lanterns, and string lights creates a soft, cosy glow.</li>
</ul>
Whether it's a bedroom in your main home or a guest room in a vacation retreat, boho interiors make every space feel welcoming and full of personality. Homeowners frequently ask <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/can-different-rooms-have-different-interior-design-styles/">can different rooms have different interior design styles</a>, and a vibrant boho guest suite within an otherwise neutral home is an ideal way to experiment.
<h2>3. Cottage Interior Design: Timeless &amp; Cosy Charm</h2>
If you love interiors that feel warm, rustic, and nostalgic, cottage interior design is the perfect choice. When renovating heritage properties, exploring layouts like <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/open-plan-or-separate-rooms-victorian-terrace/">open plan or separate rooms in Victorian terrace</a> homes allows you to retain character while enjoying modern comfort.

<strong>Warm &amp; Inviting Colour Schemes</strong>
<ul>
 	<li>Stick to soft pastels, muted greens, creams, and warm neutrals to create a classic cottage feel.</li>
 	<li>Floral and gingham patterns, particularly on curtains and cushions, add a quaint, traditional touch.</li>
</ul>
<strong>Classic Cottage Furnishings</strong>
<ul>
 	<li>Exposed wooden beams and distressed furniture instantly add to the rustic charm.</li>
 	<li>Cosy, overstuffed armchairs and vintage-style beds make rooms feel inviting and timeless.</li>
 	<li>A farmhouse-style dining table with mismatched chairs adds character to the heart of the home.</li>
</ul>
<strong>Decor Accents</strong>
<ul>
 	<li>Vintage ceramics, antique clocks, and handwoven baskets enhance the cottage feel.</li>
 	<li>A fireplace with a rustic mantel is the ultimate focal point for a cottage-style living room.</li>
 	<li>Fresh flowers or dried lavender in glass jars complete the look with a natural touch.</li>
</ul>
